To make factorial tail-recursive, an accumulator parameter is introduced to carry the intermediate product forward. The final computation occurs during parameter evaluation rather than after the recursive call returns:

```c
int fact_tail(int n, int acc) {
    if (n <= 1)
        return acc;
    return fact_tail(n - 1, n * acc);
}

// Helper wrapper function:
int fact(int n) {
    return fact_tail(n, 1);
}
```

In `fact_tail`, the recursive call `fact_tail(n - 1, n * acc)` is the exact last action, allowing compilers supporting tail-call optimization to reuse the current stack frame.

